  "selection": {
    "k": 1,
    "score": 5,
    "poem": "Tide\nHushed stone,\nEmber holds gloam\nEven 8721b4bd042a marks threshold\nIron breath climbs the north\nLow moss gathers around the basin\nEvery echo learns the floor by heart\nEmpty lanterns count the dust in slow spirals\nNoon fails behind the grate where tired wings rest\nLittle roots thread the old mortar with slow patient green\nA quiet weight tilts the iron bowl toward the pale morning\nUnder one roof my name becomes a narrow bright door of aurum.\n"
  },
